// ============================================================================
// VaultLaunch — XelisVault Protocol
// ============================================================================
// A serious, self-contained launchpad for XEL. Real projects only: every
// launch is filtered by a community validation vote, priced by a
// constant-product bonding curve, and held to a long-term community trust
// standard (Trusted / Untrusted). NOT a memecoin casino — the vote window is
// the quality filter, and the trust system keeps founders accountable long
// after graduation.
//
// v2.0 — TWO-PATH GRADUATION: a founder who locks serious liquidity from day
// one (>= direct_listing_threshold) graduates DIRECTLY (D7); smaller floats
// discover price on the bonding curve first. Graduation is worth reaching:
// graduated projects trade at a LOWER fee (D8) and the team allocation
// unlocks (D3). A small migration fee is taken from the curve once, at
// graduation (D9).
//
// v3.0 — FULL PROPOSAL DATA: the vote happens with EVERYTHING on the table
// (D10): the creator declares a vesting plan AT PROPOSITION TIME and the
// contract enforces it at graduation — the community votes on the exact
// unlock schedule it will get, not a promise. Projects carry SOCIAL LINKS
// (Twitter / Telegram / Discord, D11) the team can update at any time. And
// the contract itself keeps the market's scoreboard (D12): per-project
// buy/sell volume, trade count, last trade topoheight, spot market cap,
// all-time-high market cap and the market cap at graduation are all
// calculated and STORED on-chain — no indexer required to know how a token
// is doing.
//
// ZERO inter-contract calls. ZERO external dependencies. ONE file.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// DESIGN DECISIONS (and why — read before changing anything)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// D1. Tokens are an INTERNAL LEDGER inside this contract. XELIS smart
//     contracts cannot call each other today, so a launched token cannot be
//     a separately deployed contract the launchpad controls. Each project's
//     token lives as per-address balances in this contract's storage and
//     trades ONLY against its bonding curve here. The day the VM ships
//     inter-contract calls, migrations to an external DEX become possible;
//     until then this contract IS the pool a graduated project "migrates"
//     onto.
//
// D2. Graduation does NOT stop trading. There is no external DEX to migrate
//     to (see D1), so freezing the curve at graduation would trap holders.
//     Instead: the bonding PHASE ends (the launch milestone), the project
//     becomes Graduated + Trusted, and the same constant-product math keeps
//     serving trades forever — at the REDUCED graduated fee (D8). The
//     contract IS the token's permanent venue.
//
// D3. Team tokens are RESERVED from day one and CLAIMED after graduation.
//     The curve's sellable supply excludes the team allocation from day one,
//     so the allocation can never be over-sold. Once the project graduates,
//     the creator chooses: claim the full allocation immediately (the
//     migration reward) OR lock it into a linear vesting (a public
//     commitment signal — visible to every buyer via get_team_allocation).
//     A project that never graduates does not hold the team hostage: after
//     team_unlock_delay (~6 months) of bonding, the creator may claim the
//     allocation late, so a slow start never becomes a dead loss. Claims are
//     debited against a running team_paid counter — the allocation is paid
//     EXACTLY once across all paths (I4).
//
// D4. Losing trust blocks BUYS, never SELLs. When a project is Untrusted,
//     new buys are refused (protecting new entrants — the entire point of
//     the trust system) but holders can always exit. A trust flip can never
//     trap funds.
//
// D5. Fees ACCRUE and are pulled by withdraw_fees(). Submission, trading,
//     migration and recovery fees accumulate in `pending_fees`; the admin
//     withdraws them capped at what the contract can spare after covering
//     every curve's reserves and every refundable rejection. 100% of revenue
//     goes to the admin — nothing is burned.
//
// D6. Voting is 1 address = 1 vote, per voting round. Every vote costs a
//     network fee — that is the only (and honest) sybil cost on XELIS today.
//     Votes reset when a new validation round opens; trust tallies otherwise
//     accumulate for the whole life of the project.
//
// D7. TWO-PATH GRADUATION (the liquidity cap). A founder may lock ANY
//     liquidity >= min_liquidity; whether the project skips the bonding
//     phase is decided by the DIRECT LISTING THRESHOLD, an admin-tunable
//     cap (default 2000 XEL — what a 500 XEL float graduates at under the
//     default x4 multiplier). Liquidity >= threshold at propose time means
//     the project graduates the moment validation passes: a "migration to
//     the pool" on day one (deep reserves, graduated fee, Trusted badge,
//     team unlock — the full set of graduation advantages, immediately).
//     Below the threshold: the classic bonding curve and its price
//     discovery. The threshold is snapshotted per project at propose time
//     (founders get the rules they signed up for, whatever the admin tunes
//     later), and it can never undercut min_liquidity (cross-checked
//     setters).
//
// D8. GRADUATION PAYS. Graduated projects trade at graduated_fee_bps
//     (default 0.25%), not trading_fee_bps (default 0.50% while bonding).
//     The setters cross-check graduated_fee_bps <= trading_fee_bps and the
//     fee helper re-clamps at read time, so the graduation discount can
//     never be inverted by any parameter combination. The discount is
//     acquired at graduation and survives a later trust loss (holders exit
//     cheap; the milestone is what is rewarded, not ongoing behaviour).
//
// D9. MIGRATION FEE — protocol revenue at migration, pump.fun-style but
//     small: when a project graduates — by curve growth OR by direct
//     listing — migration_fee_bps (default 0.5%) is taken ONCE from the
//     project's curve reserves and accrues to pending_fees (admin revenue,
//     D5). Reserves dip by exactly that fee and every subsequent trade
//     prices it in. Charged on the reserves AT the graduation moment, so a
//     direct listing pays it on its seed liquidity and a curve graduate on
//     its (>= 4x larger) grown reserves.
//
// D10. VESTING PLAN AT PROPOSITION — the votable commitment. propose() takes
//     a vesting_duration: 0 means "team claims at graduation" (the classic
//     migration reward), any value inside the admin-bounded window
//     [vesting_min, vesting_max] is a DECLARED PLAN that the contract
//     BINDS at graduation: graduate() starts the linear vesting
//     automatically with exactly that duration. The community votes with
//     the unlock schedule on the table (get_proposal_data exposes it before
//     a single vote is cast); a creator cannot water the commitment down
//     afterwards — start_team_vesting refuses planned projects ("planned")
//     because the plan IS the vesting. The plan is validated against the
//     bounds snapshotted at propose time (founders get the rules they
//     signed up for, D7-consistent) and only binds at graduation: a project
//     that never graduates falls back to the late-claim path (D3) — after
//     ~6 months of bonding the allocation is claimable, plan or no plan.
//
// D11. SOCIAL LINKS — mutable project metadata. Twitter, Telegram and
//     Discord links are part of the proposal (empty = "no link") and can be
//     updated by the creator AT ANY TIME via update_project_info, exactly
//     like description/website/logo: communities move, channels get
//     rebuilt, and a launchpad that freezes social pointers forces teams
//     to abandon their own project page. Length-capped display metadata,
//     same trust model as the website field — the frontend renders, the
//     voters judge. Name/symbol/supply/team stay immutable (structural).
//
// D12. ON-CHAIN TRADING DATA — the contract keeps the scoreboard itself.
//     Every buy/sell records: directional volumes (buy_volume = attached
//     XEL, sell_volume = pre-fee gross out), the running total, the trade
//     count, the last trade topoheight — per project AND protocol-wide —
//     plus the spot market cap recomputed and STORED after every trade, its
//     all-time high (only ever grows), and the market cap snapshotted at
//     graduation (the milestone number). All via record_trade() and
//     update_market_cap(), all additions overflow-guarded (checked_add).
//     The stored spot value can never drift from the live one: it is
//     rewritten by the same formula after every state change of the curve.
//     get_market_cap stays a pure recompute (never trusts storage);
//     get_market_cap_history exposes the stored series.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// LIFECYCLE (status codes)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   0 Validation  project submitted; support/report window is open
//                 (ends at validation_end topoheight; outcome applied by
//                  finalize_validation, callable by ANYONE after the window)
//       ├── pass (>= min_participants voters AND >= 80% support)
//       │     ├── liquidity >= direct_listing_threshold ──> 3 Graduated
//       │     │     (direct listing: skip bonding; migration fee taken;
//       │     │      graduated fee; Trusted badge; team unlock — D7/D8/D9)
//       │     └── else ──> 2 Bonding (curve is live)
//       └── fail ──> 1 Rejected ──> claim_refund() returns 100% of the
//                                    founder's liquidity, once
//   2 Bonding     curve is live: buy() / sell(); votes continue and can
//                 flip the project Untrusted (see D4)
//                 graduation when reserves >= liquidity * multiplier
//                 ──> 3 Graduated (+ Trusted): migration fee taken (D9),
//                     team allocation claimable (D3), trading continues at
//                     the graduated fee (D2/D8), trust votes keep going
//   5 Untrusted   reports reached the loss threshold while Bonding/
//                 Graduated/Trusted: buys blocked, sells open, votes open
//                 recovery: request_revalidation() by the creator —
//                   * not graduated: free, normal thresholds
//                   * graduated: pays recovery_fee (default 250 XEL to the
//                     admin) and must pass STRICTER thresholds
//                   ──> 6 Recovery window ──> pass: 2 (Bonding) or 4 (Trusted)
//                                             fail: back to 5 (retryable)
//   4 Trusted     recovered status for graduated projects (same trading
//                 rules as Graduated)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// BONDING-CURVE MATH (constant product, integer, contract-favouring floors)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// State per project: R = real XEL reserves, C = curve token supply
// (sellable balance held by the curve). Price = R / C.
//
//   buy  with X XEL attached:      fee = X * fee_bps / 10000
//                                  net = X - fee                  (joins R)
//                                  tokens_out = C * net / (R + net)
//   sell of T tokens:             gross = R * T / (C + T)         (leaves R)
//                                  fee  = gross * fee_bps / 10000
//                                  out  = gross - fee              (to caller)
//
//   fee_bps = current_fee_bps(graduated): graduated_fee_bps once the
//   project has graduated (D8, clamped <= trading_fee_bps), else
//   trading_fee_bps. Buy, sell AND both quotes use the same helper, so a
//   quote can never disagree with the trade it previews.
//
// Both directions floor (integer division) in favour of the contract, so the
// pool can never go insolvent from rounding. All intermediates are computed
// in u128 (products are up to 1e31; u64 would overflow).
//
// Graduation (curve path): R >= liquidity_deposited * graduation_multiplier
// (u128 compare), checked after every buy while Bonding. At that moment
// take_migration_fee() applies: fee = fee_take(R, migration_fee_bps);
// R -= fee; pending_fees += fee (D9).
//
// Team unlock (D3): unlocked =
//   vesting active (vs > 0) : team * (topo - vs) / vd   (linear, floored)
//   graduated, no vesting   : team                      (immediate full)
//   bonding >= team_delay   : team                      (late full claim)
//   otherwise               : 0
// claimable = unlocked - team_paid (paid EXACTLY once across paths — I4).
//
// Market cap = R * (total_supply - C - team_remaining) / C (u128, saturating)
// where team_remaining = team_alloc - team_paid. Stored per project after
// every trade (mc), its all-time high (mh) and the graduation snapshot (mg)
// are updated by update_market_cap / graduate (D12).
//
// Volume (D12): buy_volume sums the ATTACHED XEL of every buy (fee
// included, like an exchange's quote-side volume), sell_volume sums the
// PRE-FEE gross XEL out of every sell, total volume = buy + sell. Kept per
// project (bv/sv/vo) and protocol-wide (tbv/tsv/tvl), with trade counts
// (tc/ttc) and the last trade topoheight (lt). I9 keeps the identity
// vo == bv + sv exact at all times.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// FEES (defaults — ALL admin-configurable, ALL revenue to the admin)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   submission_fee             10 XEL     paid once per proposal (non-refundable)
//   min_liquidity            500 XEL     founder's locked seed liquidity
//   trading_fee_bps             50 bps    on every buy and sell while bonding
//   graduated_fee_bps           25 bps    once graduated (<= trading fee, D8)
//   migration_fee_bps           50 bps    taken ONCE from reserves at
//                                         graduation (D9), on both paths
//   direct_listing_threshold 2000 XEL     liquidity that skips bonding (D7)
//   recovery_fee              250 XEL     to re-open validation after trust
//                                         loss on a GRADUATED project
//   team_unlock_delay    3153600 topos    ~6 months of bonding before a
//                                         never-graduated team may claim (D3)
//   vesting bounds  518400..6307200 topos creator-chosen linear vesting
//                                         (~1 month .. ~1 year, admin-bounded)
//   validation window      51840 topos  ~3 days at ~5s per topoheight
//   min_participants            20      minimum voters to validate a project
//   min_approval_ratio_bps    8000      80% support required
//   graduation_multiplier        4      graduate at 4x the deposited liquidity
//   recovery_min_participants   40      stricter recovery quorum
//   recovery_min_ratio_bps     9000     90% support to recover Trust
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// SECURITY MODEL (honest threat documentation)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   * The admin is a hot role: it sets every fee/parameter and can pause NEW
//     proposals and NEW buys. It can NEVER move curve reserves, user token
//     balances, or refundable rejections — withdraw_fees() is capped at
//     pending_fees and at the contract's uncommitted balance. Sells, votes,
//     refunds and finalization are NEVER pausable: exits and community
//     decisions cannot be frozen.
//   * Fee parameters are CROSS-CHECKED pairs: graduated_fee_bps <=
//     trading_fee_bps (the graduation discount can never invert, D8) and
//     direct_listing_threshold >= min_liquidity (the fast track can never
//     swallow every proposal, D7). Both setters read the partner value; the
//     fee helper re-clamps defensively at every use.
//   * Voting sybil-resistance is the network fee, nothing more (documented,
//     not hidden). min_participants and the 80% bar make cheap attack
//     campaigns expensive: 20+ voting transactions, each paying network fees.
//   * Params are range-checked on every setter (hard caps in constants):
//     trading/graduated fees can never exceed 10%, the migration fee can
//     never exceed 5%, ratios stay in (50%..100%], durations and multipliers
//     stay sane. A compromised admin can hurt the fee model, not the funds.
//   * No reentrancy surface: XELIS invokes are atomic and this contract
//     calls no other contract.
//   * Front-running buys/sells is possible (no mempool privacy) — same as
//     every public DEX on XELIS today; quotes are view functions, use them.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// INVARIANTS
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   I1. Ledger: curve_supply + sum(balances) + team_remaining
//       == total_supply, for every project, always — where
//       team_remaining = team_alloc - team_paid. Team tokens enter balances
//       ONLY through claim_team_allocation (graduation path or delayed
//       path), always debited from team_paid.
//   I2. Solvency: contract XEL balance >= total_curve_xel + pending_fees +
//       locked_refunds, before and after every entry. The migration fee
//       moves value from a curve's reserves into pending_fees without
//       touching total_curve_xel — safe because every live project's seed
//       liquidity sits uncommitted in the balance (it only ever leaves as a
//       rejected refund, which is locked_refunds; and the fee is a small
//       fraction of that seed). Checked in withdraw_fees (the only exit
//       path for fees).
//   I3. A project's reserves can only grow by buy nets and shrink by sell
//       grosses and the one-time migration fee; the founder's liquidity only
//       leaves via claim_refund on a Rejected project, exactly once.
//   I4. Team tokens are paid to the creator EXACTLY once across all claim
//       paths: every claim adds unlocked - team_paid and team_paid only ever
//       increases, capped at team_alloc.
//   I5. Every vote is one storage key ("v:{id}:{round}:{addr}"); an address
//       votes at most once per round; rounds only increase.
//   I6. Status transitions are one-way per path (see LIFECYCLE); nobody,
//       including the admin, can jump states arbitrarily.
//   I7. All transfers are checked (no swallowed failures). Every panic
//       message is a fixed short literal (no user data in panics).
//   I8. Untrusted blocks buys ONLY (D4) — sells and refunds always work.
//   I9. Volume identity: per project, vo == bv + sv at ALL times (vo only
//       grows through record_trade, once per trade, by exactly the recorded
//       amount); protocol-wide, tvl == tbv + tsv. The stored market cap mc
//       is refreshed by update_market_cap after EVERY change of its inputs
//       (buy, sell, graduation fee, team claim), so it always equals the
//       recomputed R * circulating / C; mh only ever grows, and mg is
//       written exactly once, at graduation.
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// STORAGE MAP (string keys, flat KV — house style)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//   Global   : adm pc sub mnl tfe gfe mgf dlt mnp mab vdt gmu tdy vmn vmx
//              rfe rmp rmr pfe fcl tvl tcx lrf pz xa tbv tsv ttc
//              (see constants below)
//   Project  : p:{id}:cr creator        p:{id}:st status (u64)
//              p:{id}:nm name           p:{id}:sy symbol
//              p:{id}:ds description    p:{id}:ws website
//              p:{id}:lg logo           p:{id}:tw twitter   (D11)
//              p:{id}:tg telegram       p:{id}:dc discord   (D11)
//              p:{id}:ts total_supply   p:{id}:tb team_bps
//              p:{id}:lq liquidity deposited
//              p:{id}:rv curve reserves p:{id}:cs curve token supply
//              p:{id}:ct created topo   p:{id}:ve validation deadline
//              p:{id}:sp supports       p:{id}:rp reports
//              p:{id}:gr graduated      p:{id}:rc refund claimed
//              p:{id}:rd vote round     p:{id}:vo trade volume (total)
//              p:{id}:dl direct-listing p:{id}:bt bonding start topo
//              p:{id}:tp team paid      p:{id}:vs vesting start topo
//              p:{id}:vd vesting duration
//              p:{id}:vp vesting PLAN declared at propose (D10)
//              p:{id}:bv buy volume     p:{id}:sv sell volume (D12)
//              p:{id}:tc trade count    p:{id}:lt last trade topo
//              p:{id}:mc market cap (stored spot, D12)
//              p:{id}:mh market cap ATH p:{id}:mg market cap at graduation
//   Votes    : v:{id}:{round}:{addr} -> bool
//   Balances : b:{id}:{addr}          -> u64 (token atomic units, 8 dec)
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// EVENTS (V6 contract events: id + array of string fields)
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
//    1 ProjectCreated      [id, name, symbol, liquidity]
//    2 ProjectSupported    [id, round, voter]
//    3 ProjectReported     [id, round, voter]
//    4 ValidationFinished  [id, "1"|"0"]
//    5 BondingOpened       [id]
//    6 TokensBought        [id, xel_in, tokens_out, fee]
//    7 TokensSold          [id, tokens_in, xel_out, fee]
//    8 ProjectGraduated    [id, reserves, team_allocation]
//    9 TrustLost           [id, reports, supports]
//   10 TrustRecovered      [id]
//   11 FeesCollected       [amount]
//   12 ParamSet            [param, value]
//   13 Paused              ["admin"]        14 Unpaused ["admin"]
//   15 AdminSet            [new_admin]
//   16 RefundClaimed       [id, amount]
//   17 RecoveryRequested   [id, round]
//   18 ProjectInfoUpdated  [id]
//   19 TeamVestingStarted  [id, duration]
//   20 TeamClaimed         [id, amount]
//   21 DirectListed        [id, liquidity]
//   22 MigrationFeeTaken   [id, fee]
//
// ----------------------------------------------------------------------------
// CHUNK TABLE (entry-point IDs, 0-based, declaration order — CI-checked)
//    0   constructor                   1   only_admin                    2   require_project
//    3   proj_key                      4   vote_key                      5   bal_key
//    6   fee_take                      7   buy_tokens_out                8   sell_xel_out
//    9   team_alloc_of                 10  trust_guard                   11  graduate
//    12  take_migration_fee            13  current_fee_bps               14  team_remaining
//    15  team_unlocked                 16  propose                       17  support
//    18  report                        19  finalize_validation           20  buy
//    21  sell                          22  claim_refund                  23  request_revalidation
//    24  update_project_info           25  start_team_vesting            26  claim_team_allocation
//    27  set_submission_fee            28  set_trading_fee               29  set_graduated_trading_fee
//    30  set_migration_fee             31  set_direct_listing_threshold  32  set_min_liquidity
//    33  set_min_participants          34  set_min_approval_ratio        35  set_validation_duration
//    36  set_graduation_multiplier     37  set_team_unlock_delay         38  set_vesting_bounds
//    39  set_recovery_fee              40  set_recovery_params           41  set_admin
//    42  set_paused                    43  withdraw_fees                 44  checked_add
//    45  update_market_cap             46  record_trade                  47  get_project
//    48  get_project_info              49  get_project_status            50  get_project_tokenomics
//    51  get_project_trust             52  get_bonding_info              53  get_current_price
//    54  get_buy_quote                 55  get_sell_quote                56  get_market_cap
//    57  get_token_balance             58  has_voted                     59  get_total_projects
//    60  get_projects_by_status        61  get_project_by_rank           62  get_latest_projects
//    63  get_trusted_projects          64  get_trusted_by_rank           65  get_team_allocation
//    66  get_protocol_stats            67  get_config                    68  get_recovery_config
//    69  get_team_config               70  get_social_links              71  get_trading_stats
//    72  get_market_cap_history        73  get_proposal_data             74  get_volume_stats
//    75  get_status_label              76  get_version
//
//   Auto-verified by scripts/verify_chunk_ids.py on every push: the table
//   above MUST match the declaration order in this file. Renumbering any
//   function invalidates the table — regenerate it, never hand-edit around.
// ============================================================================

const VERSION: string = "VaultLaunch v3.0.0"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Status codes (see LIFECYCLE)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const ST_VALIDATION: u64 = 0
const ST_REJECTED: u64 = 1
const ST_BONDING: u64 = 2
const ST_GRADUATED: u64 = 3
const ST_TRUSTED: u64 = 4
const ST_UNTRUSTED: u64 = 5
const ST_RECOVERY: u64 = 6

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Global capacity (storage growth bound; also the static loop bound of the
// listing views — R8-clean)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MAX_PROJECTS: u64 = 8192

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Defaults (atomic units, 8 decimals — 1 XEL = 100000000)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const DEFAULT_SUBMISSION_FEE: u64 = 1000000000
const DEFAULT_MIN_LIQUIDITY: u64 = 50000000000
const DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS: u64 = 50
const DEFAULT_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS: u64 = 25
const DEFAULT_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS: u64 = 50
const DEFAULT_DIRECT_LISTING: u64 = 200000000000
const DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS: u64 = 20
const DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS: u64 = 8000
const DEFAULT_VALIDATION_TOPO: u64 = 51840
const DEFAULT_GRAD_MULTIPLIER: u64 = 4
const DEFAULT_RECOVERY_FEE: u64 = 25000000000
const DEFAULT_RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS: u64 = 40
const DEFAULT_RECOVERY_RATIO_BPS: u64 = 9000
const DEFAULT_TEAM_DELAY: u64 = 3153600
const DEFAULT_VESTING_MIN: u64 = 518400
const DEFAULT_VESTING_MAX: u64 = 6307200

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Hard caps for admin parameters (a compromised admin can hurt the fee
// model, never the funds)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MAX_SUBMISSION_FEE: u64 = 10000000000
const MIN_LIQUIDITY_FLOOR: u64 = 100000000
const MAX_MIN_LIQUIDITY: u64 = 10000000000000
const MAX_TRADING_FEE_BPS: u64 = 1000
const MAX_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS: u64 = 1000
const MAX_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS: u64 = 500
const MAX_DIRECT_LISTING: u64 = 1000000000000000
const MAX_PARTICIPANTS: u64 = 100000
const MIN_RATIO_BPS: u64 = 5001
const MIN_VALIDATION_TOPO: u64 = 720
const MAX_VALIDATION_TOPO: u64 = 259200
const MIN_GRAD_MULTIPLIER: u64 = 2
const MAX_GRAD_MULTIPLIER: u64 = 100
const MAX_RECOVERY_FEE: u64 = 100000000000
const MIN_TEAM_DELAY_TOPO: u64 = 86400
const MAX_TEAM_DELAY_TOPO: u64 = 12614400
const VESTING_FLOOR_TOPO: u64 = 17280
const VESTING_CEIL_TOPO: u64 = 12614400

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Per-project caps (checked in propose)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MIN_TOTAL_SUPPLY: u64 = 100000000
const MAX_TOTAL_SUPPLY: u64 = 10000000000000000
const MAX_TEAM_BPS: u64 = 2000
const MAX_NAME_LEN: u32 = 64
const MAX_SYMBOL_LEN: u32 = 16
const MAX_DESC_LEN: u32 = 512
const MAX_URL_LEN: u32 = 256

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Trade guards (dust & overflow containment)
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const MIN_BUY_XEL: u64 = 1000000
const MAX_TRADE_XEL: u64 = 10000000000000
const MAX_LIQUIDITY: u64 = 1000000000000000

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Math helpers
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const BPS_DENOM: u64 = 10000
const PRICE_SCALE: u64 = 100000000
const U64_MAX: u64 = 18446744073709551615
const U64_MAX_128: u128 = 18446744073709551615u128

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Global storage keys
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const ADMIN_KEY: string = "adm"
const COUNT_KEY: string = "pc"
const SUBMISSION_FEE_KEY: string = "sub"
const MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY: string = "mnl"
const TRADING_FEE_KEY: string = "tfe"
const GRADUATED_FEE_KEY: string = "gfe"
const MIGRATION_FEE_KEY: string = "mgf"
const DIRECT_LISTING_KEY: string = "dlt"
const MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY: string = "mnp"
const MIN_APPROVAL_KEY: string = "mab"
const VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY: string = "vdt"
const GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY: string = "gmu"
const TEAM_DELAY_KEY: string = "tdy"
const VESTING_MIN_KEY: string = "vmn"
const VESTING_MAX_KEY: string = "vmx"
const RECOVERY_FEE_KEY: string = "rfe"
const RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS_KEY: string = "rmp"
const RECOVERY_RATIO_KEY: string = "rmr"
const PENDING_FEES_KEY: string = "pfe"
const FEES_LIFETIME_KEY: string = "fcl"
const TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY: string = "tvl"
const TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY: string = "tcx"
const LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY: string = "lrf"
const PAUSED_KEY: string = "pz"
const XEL_ASSET_KEY: string = "xa"
const TOTAL_BUY_VOL_KEY: string = "tbv"
const TOTAL_SELL_VOL_KEY: string = "tsv"
const TOTAL_TRADES_KEY: string = "ttc"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Project field keys (p:{id}:{field})
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const F_CREATOR: string = "cr"
const F_STATUS: string = "st"
const F_NAME: string = "nm"
const F_SYMBOL: string = "sy"
const F_DESC: string = "ds"
const F_WEBSITE: string = "ws"
const F_LOGO: string = "lg"
const F_SUPPLY: string = "ts"
const F_TEAM_BPS: string = "tb"
const F_LIQUIDITY: string = "lq"
const F_RESERVES: string = "rv"
const F_CURVE: string = "cs"
const F_CREATED: string = "ct"
const F_DEADLINE: string = "ve"
const F_SUPPORTS: string = "sp"
const F_REPORTS: string = "rp"
const F_GRADUATED: string = "gr"
const F_REFUND: string = "rc"
const F_ROUND: string = "rd"
const F_VOLUME: string = "vo"
const F_DL: string = "dl"
const F_BONDING_START: string = "bt"
const F_TEAM_PAID: string = "tp"
const F_VESTING_START: string = "vs"
const F_VESTING_DURATION: string = "vd"
const F_VESTING_PLAN: string = "vp"
const F_TWITTER: string = "tw"
const F_TELEGRAM: string = "tg"
const F_DISCORD: string = "dc"
const F_BUY_VOL: string = "bv"
const F_SELL_VOL: string = "sv"
const F_TRADES: string = "tc"
const F_LAST_TRADE: string = "lt"
const F_MCAP: string = "mc"
const F_MCAP_HIGH: string = "mh"
const F_MCAP_GRAD: string = "mg"

const PROJ_PREFIX: string = "p:"
const VOTE_PREFIX: string = "v:"
const BAL_PREFIX: string = "b:"

// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Event IDs
// ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
const EV_PROJECT_CREATED: u64 = 1
const EV_SUPPORTED: u64 = 2
const EV_REPORTED: u64 = 3
const EV_VALIDATION_FINISHED: u64 = 4
const EV_BONDING_OPENED: u64 = 5
const EV_TOKENS_BOUGHT: u64 = 6
const EV_TOKENS_SOLD: u64 = 7
const EV_PROJECT_GRADUATED: u64 = 8
const EV_TRUST_LOST: u64 = 9
const EV_TRUST_RECOVERED: u64 = 10
const EV_FEES_COLLECTED: u64 = 11
const EV_PARAM_SET: u64 = 12
const EV_PAUSED: u64 = 13
const EV_UNPAUSED: u64 = 14
const EV_ADMIN_SET: u64 = 15
const EV_REFUND_CLAIMED: u64 = 16
const EV_RECOVERY_REQUESTED: u64 = 17
const EV_PROJECT_INFO_UPDATED: u64 = 18
const EV_TEAM_VESTING_STARTED: u64 = 19
const EV_TEAM_CLAIMED: u64 = 20
const EV_DIRECT_LISTED: u64 = 21
const EV_MIGRATION_FEE: u64 = 22

// ============================================================================
// 0. CONSTRUCTOR
// ============================================================================
// Admin = deployer (signer of the deployment transaction). All parameters
// start at their documented defaults; the admin adjusts them with the
// set_* entries (range-checked against the hard caps, cross-checked in
// pairs — see SECURITY).
// ============================================================================
hook constructor() -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()

    let deployer: Address = Transaction::current().unwrap().source()
    s.store(ADMIN_KEY, deployer)

    s.store(COUNT_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(SUBMISSION_FEE_KEY, DEFAULT_SUBMISSION_FEE)
    s.store(MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY, DEFAULT_MIN_LIQUIDITY)
    s.store(TRADING_FEE_KEY, DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS)
    s.store(GRADUATED_FEE_KEY, DEFAULT_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS)
    s.store(MIGRATION_FEE_KEY, DEFAULT_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS)
    s.store(DIRECT_LISTING_KEY, DEFAULT_DIRECT_LISTING)
    s.store(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY, DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS)
    s.store(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY, DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS)
    s.store(VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY, DEFAULT_VALIDATION_TOPO)
    s.store(GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY, DEFAULT_GRAD_MULTIPLIER)
    s.store(TEAM_DELAY_KEY, DEFAULT_TEAM_DELAY)
    s.store(VESTING_MIN_KEY, DEFAULT_VESTING_MIN)
    s.store(VESTING_MAX_KEY, DEFAULT_VESTING_MAX)
    s.store(RECOVERY_FEE_KEY, DEFAULT_RECOVERY_FEE)
    s.store(RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS_KEY, DEFAULT_RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS)
    s.store(RECOVERY_RATIO_KEY, DEFAULT_RECOVERY_RATIO_BPS)

    s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(FEES_LIFETIME_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(TOTAL_BUY_VOL_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(TOTAL_SELL_VOL_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(TOTAL_TRADES_KEY, 0u64)
    s.store(PAUSED_KEY, false)

    s.store(XEL_ASSET_KEY, get_xelis_asset())

    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// INTERNAL HELPERS
// ============================================================================

// 1. Access control — every admin entry funnels through this.
fn only_admin() {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let admin_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(ADMIN_KEY)
    require(admin_opt.is_some(), "noadmin")
    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let admin: Address = admin_opt.expect("guarded")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == admin, "notauth")
}

// 2. Project existence — every project-scoped entry and view starts here.
fn require_project(pid: u64) {
    let count: u64 = Storage::new().load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    require(pid < count, "noproj")
}

// 3. Storage key of a project field: "p:{id}:{field}".
fn proj_key(pid: u64, field: string) -> string {
    return PROJ_PREFIX + pid.to_string(10u32) + ":" + field
}

// 4. Storage key of a vote marker: "v:{id}:{round}:{addr}".
//    One key per (project, round, voter) — I5.
fn vote_key(pid: u64, round: u64, voter: Address) -> string {
    return VOTE_PREFIX + pid.to_string(10u32) + ":" + round.to_string(10u32) + ":" + voter.to_string()
}

// 5. Storage key of a token balance: "b:{id}:{addr}".
fn bal_key(pid: u64, owner: Address) -> string {
    return BAL_PREFIX + pid.to_string(10u32) + ":" + owner.to_string()
}

// 6. Fee split — floor, in favour of the contract.
fn fee_take(amount: u64, bps: u64) -> u64 {
    let wide: u128 = (amount as u128) * (bps as u128) / (BPS_DENOM as u128)
    return wide as u64
}

// 7. Curve buy math: tokens out for a NET xel amount (fee already removed).
//    tokens_out = C * net / (R + net), floored. Always < C.
fn buy_tokens_out(reserves: u64, curve_supply: u64, net_xel: u64) -> u64 {
    let wide: u128 = (curve_supply as u128) * (net_xel as u128) / ((reserves as u128) + (net_xel as u128))
    return wide as u64
}

// 8. Curve sell math: XEL out (gross, before fee) for T tokens.
//    gross = R * T / (C + T), floored. Always < R.
fn sell_xel_out(reserves: u64, curve_supply: u64, tokens: u64) -> u64 {
    let wide: u128 = (reserves as u128) * (tokens as u128) / ((curve_supply as u128) + (tokens as u128))
    return wide as u64
}

// 9. Team allocation of a project (atomic token units), reserved in the
//    curve from day one, paid out via claim_team_allocation (I1, I4).
fn team_alloc_of(total_supply: u64, team_bps: u64) -> u64 {
    let wide: u128 = (total_supply as u128) * (team_bps as u128) / (BPS_DENOM as u128)
    return wide as u64
}

// 10. TRUST GUARD — evaluated after every vote on a project that already
//     trades (Bonding / Graduated / Trusted). When reports reach the loss
//     threshold (same bar as validation: quorum + ratio), the project flips
//     to Untrusted: buys blocked, sells and votes stay open (D4).
fn trust_guard(pid: u64, status: u64) {
    if status == ST_BONDING || status == ST_GRADUATED || status == ST_TRUSTED {
        let s: Storage = Storage::new()
        let supports: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
        let reports: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
        let total: u64 = supports + reports
        let min_p: u64 = s.load(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS)
        let ratio: u64 = s.load(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS)
        if total >= min_p {
            if (reports as u128) * 10000u128 >= (ratio as u128) * (total as u128) {
                s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_UNTRUSTED)
                emit_event(EV_TRUST_LOST, [pid.to_string(10u32), reports.to_string(10u32), supports.to_string(10u32)])
            }
        }
    }
}

// 11. GRADUATE — flips a trading project to Graduated (the milestone), then
//     takes the one-time migration fee from the curve (D9), BINDS the
//     declared vesting plan if there is one (D10), and snapshots the
//     graduation market cap (D12). Team tokens are NOT minted here: they
//     become claimable (immediately, or through the plan's linear stream)
//     via claim_team_allocation (D3). Called from buy() when the curve
//     crossed the graduation threshold, and from finalize_validation() for
//     a direct listing (both paths converge here — one set of
//     post-graduation rules).
fn graduate(pid: u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()

    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_GRADUATED)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED), true)

    take_migration_fee(pid)

    // D10 — bind the declared vesting plan: the community voted on this
    // exact schedule; graduate() is where it becomes real. Irreversible by
    // design (start_team_vesting refuses planned projects afterwards).
    let plan: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_PLAN)).unwrap_or(0)
    if plan > 0 {
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START), get_current_topoheight())
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_DURATION), plan)
        emit_event(EV_TEAM_VESTING_STARTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), plan.to_string(10u32)])
    }

    // D12 — the milestone number: market cap recomputed AFTER the migration
    // fee (the honest post-graduation state), stored as the graduation cap.
    update_market_cap(pid)
    let cap: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_GRAD), cap)

    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team_bps: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team: u64 = team_alloc_of(total_supply, team_bps)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    emit_event(EV_PROJECT_GRADUATED, [pid.to_string(10u32), reserves.to_string(10u32), team.to_string(10u32)])
}

// 12. MIGRATION FEE (D9) — taken ONCE per project, at graduation (both
//     paths, via graduate()). fee = fee_take(reserves, migration_fee_bps)
//     leaves the curve's reserves and accrues to pending_fees. Safe for I2:
//     total_curve_xel is untouched and the project's seed liquidity (never
//     withdrawable except as a locked refund) covers the fee many times
//     over. No-op when the fee rate is zero.
fn take_migration_fee(pid: u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let bps: u64 = s.load(MIGRATION_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS)
    if bps == 0 {
        return
    }
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let fee: u64 = fee_take(reserves, bps)
    if fee == 0 {
        return
    }
    require(reserves >= fee, "curverr")
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES), reserves - fee)
    let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending + fee)
    emit_event(EV_MIGRATION_FEE, [pid.to_string(10u32), fee.to_string(10u32)])
}

// 13. EFFECTIVE TRADING FEE (D8) — graduated projects trade at
//     graduated_fee_bps; bonding projects at trading_fee_bps. The clamp
//     guarantees graduated_fee <= trading_fee even if storage were somehow
//     inconsistent (defence in depth on top of the cross-checked setters).
//     Used by buy, sell AND both quotes — a quote can never disagree with
//     the trade it previews.
fn current_fee_bps(graduated: bool) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let bonding_fee: u64 = s.load(TRADING_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS)
    if !graduated {
        return bonding_fee
    }
    let graduated_fee: u64 = s.load(GRADUATED_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS)
    if graduated_fee > bonding_fee {
        return bonding_fee
    }
    return graduated_fee
}

// 14. Team allocation still owed to the creator: team_alloc - team_paid
//     (never negative — I4). This is the "unminted team tokens" term of I1.
fn team_remaining(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team_bps: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team: u64 = team_alloc_of(total_supply, team_bps)
    let paid: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_PAID)).unwrap_or(0)
    if paid >= team {
        return 0
    }
    return team - paid
}

// 15. TEAM UNLOCK AMOUNT (D3) — how much of the allocation the creator may
//     claim RIGHT NOW: the linear vesting stream if a vesting was started;
//     the full allocation once graduated (no vesting); the full allocation
//     for a never-graduated project after team_unlock_delay of bonding (the
//     anti-hostage late claim); zero otherwise. claim_team_allocation pays
//     unlocked - team_paid, so partial streams resume where they left off.
fn team_unlocked(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team_bps: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team: u64 = team_alloc_of(total_supply, team_bps)
    if team == 0 {
        return 0
    }

    // Linear vesting stream — the creator's voluntary commitment (D3).
    let vesting_start: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START)).unwrap_or(0)
    if vesting_start > 0 {
        let duration: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_DURATION)).unwrap_or(0)
        if duration == 0 {
            return team
        }
        let now: u64 = get_current_topoheight()
        if now <= vesting_start {
            return 0
        }
        let elapsed: u128 = (now - vesting_start) as u128
        let unlocked: u128 = (team as u128) * elapsed / (duration as u128)
        if unlocked >= (team as u128) {
            return team
        }
        return unlocked as u64
    }

    // Graduated (curve or direct listing): the migration reward (D3).
    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    if graduated {
        return team
    }

    // Never graduated but still alive after the unlock delay: the late
    // claim that keeps founders motivated (D3). Rejected/Validation
    // projects return 0 — a rejected launch never mints team tokens.
    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    if status == ST_BONDING || status == ST_UNTRUSTED || status == ST_RECOVERY {
        let bonding_start: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_BONDING_START)).unwrap_or(0)
        let delay: u64 = s.load(TEAM_DELAY_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TEAM_DELAY)
        if bonding_start > 0 {
            if (get_current_topoheight() as u128) >= (bonding_start as u128) + (delay as u128) {
                return team
            }
        }
    }
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 16. PROPOSE — submit a project to the community filter.
// ============================================================================
// @caller: the project creator (a wallet).
// @params: name, symbol, description, website, logo, twitter, telegram,
//             discord — display metadata (length-capped; social links may be
//             empty = "no link"; the team can update description, website,
//             logo AND socials at any time via update_project_info — D11);
//          total_supply — token supply in atomic units (8 decimals),
//             capped to [MIN_TOTAL_SUPPLY, MAX_TOTAL_SUPPLY];
//          team_bps — team allocation in basis points, <= 20%;
//          vesting_duration — the TEAM VESTING PLAN (D10): 0 = claim at
//             graduation (the classic reward), any value inside
//             [vesting_min, vesting_max] (SNAPSHOTTED NOW, like the
//             direct-listing threshold) is a declared plan that
//             graduate() will BIND automatically: the community votes with
//             the exact unlock schedule on the table.
// @attached: EXACTLY submission_fee + the founder's liquidity, where the
//             liquidity is >= min_liquidity and <= MAX_LIQUIDITY. The fee
//             joins pending_fees immediately (non-refundable); the liquidity
//             is locked as the curve's seed reserves.
// @returns: the project id.
// @direct listing (D7): if the locked liquidity >= direct_listing_threshold
//             (SNAPSHOTTED NOW — later admin tuning never reclassifies an
//             existing proposal), the project is flagged to graduate the
//             moment validation passes.
// @security: paused check, capacity check, metadata caps (socials included),
//            supply/team caps, plan bounds snapshot, deposit lower bound
//            (fee + min_liquidity), everything stored under fresh keys — no
//            user-controlled key material.
// ============================================================================
entry propose(name: string, symbol: string, description: string, website: string, logo: string, twitter: string, telegram: string, discord: string, total_supply: u64, team_bps: u64, vesting_duration: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(s.load(PAUSED_KEY).unwrap_or(false) == false, "paused")

    let count: u64 = s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    require(count < MAX_PROJECTS, "full")

    // Metadata caps (social links are display metadata, same rules — D11).
    require(name.len() >= 1u32 && name.len() <= MAX_NAME_LEN, "badname")
    require(symbol.len() >= 1u32 && symbol.len() <= MAX_SYMBOL_LEN, "badsym")
    require(description.len() <= MAX_DESC_LEN, "baddesc")
    require(website.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badurl")
    require(logo.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badlogo")
    require(twitter.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badtw")
    require(telegram.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badtg")
    require(discord.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "baddc")

    // Tokenomics caps.
    require(total_supply >= MIN_TOTAL_SUPPLY && total_supply <= MAX_TOTAL_SUPPLY, "badsupply")
    require(team_bps <= MAX_TEAM_BPS, "badteam")

    // Vesting plan (D10): 0 = immediate claim at graduation; otherwise it
    // must fit the admin-bounded window SNAPSHOTTED at propose time — the
    // founder gets the rules they signed up for, the community gets a plan
    // that can only be honoured, never re-tuned.
    let plan_min: u64 = s.load(VESTING_MIN_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MIN)
    let plan_max: u64 = s.load(VESTING_MAX_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MAX)
    require(vesting_duration == 0 || (vesting_duration >= plan_min && vesting_duration <= plan_max), "badplan")

    // Funds: fee (to the admin) + seed liquidity (locked in the curve).
    let sub_fee: u64 = s.load(SUBMISSION_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_SUBMISSION_FEE)
    let min_liq: u64 = s.load(MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_LIQUIDITY)
    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    let dep: u64 = get_deposit_for_asset(xel).unwrap_or(0)
    require(dep >= sub_fee + min_liq, "needliq")
    let liquidity: u64 = dep - sub_fee
    require(liquidity <= MAX_LIQUIDITY, "toobig")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let pid: u64 = count
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR), caller)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_VALIDATION)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_NAME), name)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SYMBOL), symbol)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DESC), description)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_WEBSITE), website)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_LOGO), logo)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TWITTER), twitter)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TELEGRAM), telegram)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DISCORD), discord)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY), total_supply)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS), team_bps)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY), liquidity)

    // Curve opening state: reserves = seed liquidity; the curve's sellable
    // supply EXCLUDES the team allocation (reserved until claimed — D3).
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES), liquidity)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE), total_supply - team_alloc_of(total_supply, team_bps))

    // Two-path snapshot (D7): big liquidity graduates directly at
    // validation success; the threshold is read ONCE, here.
    let threshold: u64 = s.load(DIRECT_LISTING_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_DIRECT_LISTING)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DL), liquidity >= threshold)

    // Team-claim bookkeeping (D3, D10): the declared plan rides along until
    // graduate() binds it; vs/vd stay 0 until then (or until a voluntary
    // start_team_vesting on an unplanned project).
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_PAID), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_DURATION), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_PLAN), vesting_duration)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_BONDING_START), 0u64)

    // Voting round 0 opens now.
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_CREATED), get_current_topoheight())
    let duration: u64 = s.load(VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VALIDATION_TOPO)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE), get_current_topoheight() + duration)

    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED), false)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_REFUND), false)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VOLUME), 0u64)

    // Trading-data scoreboard (D12): starts empty, filled by every trade.
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_BUY_VOL), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SELL_VOL), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TRADES), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_LAST_TRADE), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_HIGH), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_GRAD), 0u64)

    s.store(COUNT_KEY, pid + 1)

    if sub_fee > 0 {
        let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending + sub_fee)
    }

    emit_event(EV_PROJECT_CREATED, [pid.to_string(10u32), name, symbol, liquidity.to_string(10u32)])
    return pid
}

// ============================================================================
// 17. SUPPORT — vote FOR a project (validation round or ongoing trust).
// ============================================================================
// One vote per address per round (I5). During an open validation window the
// vote counts towards the pass threshold; afterwards it keeps accumulating
// in the project's trust tallies (trust_guard evaluates the flip).
// ============================================================================
entry support(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status != ST_REJECTED, "dead")
    if status == ST_VALIDATION || status == ST_RECOVERY {
        let deadline: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE)).unwrap_or(0)
        require(get_current_topoheight() < deadline, "ended")
    }

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let round: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND)).unwrap_or(0)
    let vkey: string = vote_key(pid, round, caller)
    require(s.load(vkey).unwrap_or(false) == false, "voted")
    s.store(vkey, true)

    let tally: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS), tally + 1)

    emit_event(EV_SUPPORTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), round.to_string(10u32), caller.to_string()])
    trust_guard(pid, status)
    return tally + 1
}

// ============================================================================
// 18. REPORT — vote AGAINST a project (validation round or ongoing trust).
// ============================================================================
// Mirror of support(). Enough reports on a trading project flip it to
// Untrusted (buys blocked, sells open — D4).
// ============================================================================
entry report(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status != ST_REJECTED, "dead")
    if status == ST_VALIDATION || status == ST_RECOVERY {
        let deadline: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE)).unwrap_or(0)
        require(get_current_topoheight() < deadline, "ended")
    }

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let round: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND)).unwrap_or(0)
    let vkey: string = vote_key(pid, round, caller)
    require(s.load(vkey).unwrap_or(false) == false, "voted")
    s.store(vkey, true)

    let tally: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS), tally + 1)

    emit_event(EV_REPORTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), round.to_string(10u32), caller.to_string()])
    trust_guard(pid, status)
    return tally + 1
}

// ============================================================================
// 19. FINALIZE VALIDATION — apply the outcome of a closed voting window.
// ============================================================================
// @caller: ANYONE, after the window's deadline (permissionless finalizer —
//          the outcome is fully determined by the public tallies, this only
//          executes it; the founder has a natural incentive to call it for
//          a refund on failure, the community on success).
// @rules:  initial window  : pass >= min_participants voters AND >= 80%
//                             support -> Bonding, OR direct listing when
//                             the proposal locked >= the threshold (D7):
//                             graduation on the spot (migration fee taken,
//                             graduated fee, team unlock). Fail -> Rejected
//                             (liquidity becomes refundable once).
//          recovery window : graduated projects use the STRICTER recovery
//                             thresholds; pass -> Trusted, fail -> Untrusted
// ============================================================================
entry finalize_validation(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status == ST_VALIDATION || status == ST_RECOVERY, "nowindow")
    let deadline: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(get_current_topoheight() >= deadline, "open")

    let supports: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let reports: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let total: u64 = supports + reports

    if status == ST_VALIDATION {
        let min_p: u64 = s.load(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS)
        let ratio: u64 = s.load(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS)
        if total >= min_p && (supports as u128) * 10000u128 >= (ratio as u128) * (total as u128) {
            // Trading starts now, one way or the other.
            s.store(proj_key(pid, F_BONDING_START), get_current_topoheight())
            let dl: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DL)).unwrap_or(false)
            if dl {
                // Direct listing (D7): serious liquidity skips the bonding
                // phase — graduation (and its advantages) on day one.
                graduate(pid)
                let liquidity: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0)
                emit_event(EV_VALIDATION_FINISHED, [pid.to_string(10u32), "1"])
                emit_event(EV_DIRECT_LISTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), liquidity.to_string(10u32)])
            } else {
                s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_BONDING)
                emit_event(EV_VALIDATION_FINISHED, [pid.to_string(10u32), "1"])
                emit_event(EV_BONDING_OPENED, [pid.to_string(10u32)])
            }
            return 1
        }
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_REJECTED)
        let liquidity: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0)
        let locked: u64 = s.load(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY, locked + liquidity)
        emit_event(EV_VALIDATION_FINISHED, [pid.to_string(10u32), "0"])
        return 0
    }

    // Recovery window: stricter bar for graduated projects (D-lifecycle).
    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    let min_p: u64 = s.load(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS)
    let ratio: u64 = s.load(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS)
    if graduated {
        min_p = s.load(RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS)
        ratio = s.load(RECOVERY_RATIO_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_RATIO_BPS)
    }
    if total >= min_p && (supports as u128) * 10000u128 >= (ratio as u128) * (total as u128) {
        if graduated {
            s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_TRUSTED)
        } else {
            s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_BONDING)
        }
        emit_event(EV_TRUST_RECOVERED, [pid.to_string(10u32)])
        return 1
    }
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_UNTRUSTED)
    emit_event(EV_VALIDATION_FINISHED, [pid.to_string(10u32), "0"])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 20. BUY — trade XEL for tokens on a project's curve.
// ============================================================================
// @caller: anyone (a wallet). Blocked while paused and while the project is
//          Untrusted or in a voting window (D4) — the ONLY ways buys stop.
// @attached: XEL in [MIN_BUY_XEL, MAX_TRADE_XEL]. The trading fee (bonding
//            or graduated rate, D8) goes to pending_fees; the NET amount
//            joins the reserves; tokens out follow the constant-product
//            formula (floored, u128 math).
// @returns: tokens received (atomic units).
// @graduation: if this buy pushes the reserves to
//              liquidity * graduation_multiplier while Bonding, the project
//              graduates (status flip + one-time migration fee — D9);
//              the team allocation becomes claimable (D3). Trading
//              continues (D2).
// ============================================================================
entry buy(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    require(s.load(PAUSED_KEY).unwrap_or(false) == false, "paused")

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status == ST_BONDING || status == ST_GRADUATED || status == ST_TRUSTED, "notrade")

    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    let dep: u64 = get_deposit_for_asset(xel).unwrap_or(0)
    require(dep >= MIN_BUY_XEL, "tiny")
    require(dep <= MAX_TRADE_XEL, "toobig")

    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    let bps: u64 = current_fee_bps(graduated)
    let fee: u64 = fee_take(dep, bps)
    let net: u64 = dep - fee

    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(reserves > 0 && curve_supply > 0, "empty")

    let tokens: u64 = buy_tokens_out(reserves, curve_supply, net)
    require(tokens >= 1, "tinyout")
    require(curve_supply >= tokens, "curverr")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    // Curve state (net joins reserves, tokens leave the curve).
    let new_reserves: u64 = reserves + net
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES), new_reserves)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE), curve_supply - tokens)

    // Buyer's internal ledger.
    let bkey: string = bal_key(pid, caller)
    let bal: u64 = s.load(bkey).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(bkey, bal + tokens)

    // Accounting (D12): directional + total volume, trade count, last
    // trade topo — per project and protocol-wide, all overflow-guarded.
    record_trade(pid, true, dep)
    let curve_xel: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY, curve_xel + net)
    if fee > 0 {
        let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending + fee)
    }

    emit_event(EV_TOKENS_BOUGHT, [pid.to_string(10u32), dep.to_string(10u32), tokens.to_string(10u32), fee.to_string(10u32)])

    // Graduation check (I6): only from Bonding, only once.
    if status == ST_BONDING {
        let liquidity: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0)
        let multiplier: u64 = s.load(GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRAD_MULTIPLIER)
        if (new_reserves as u128) >= (liquidity as u128) * (multiplier as u128) {
            graduate(pid)
        }
    }

    // D12 — stored market cap follows every curve state change (idempotent
    // recompute; also covers the graduation fee when it just happened).
    update_market_cap(pid)
    return tokens
}

// ============================================================================
// 21. SELL — trade tokens back for XEL. NEVER blockable (D4, I8).
// ============================================================================
// Works in Bonding, Graduated, Trusted, Untrusted AND during a recovery
// window: holders can always exit. The gross XEL leaves the reserves; the
// trading fee (graduated rate if the project graduated — D8) goes to
// pending_fees; the rest is transferred to the caller (checked transfer).
// ============================================================================
entry sell(pid: u64, token_amount: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status == ST_BONDING || status == ST_GRADUATED || status == ST_TRUSTED || status == ST_UNTRUSTED || status == ST_RECOVERY, "nosell")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    require(token_amount >= 1, "badamt")
    let bkey: string = bal_key(pid, caller)
    let bal: u64 = s.load(bkey).unwrap_or(0)
    require(bal >= token_amount, "nobal")

    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(reserves > 0 && curve_supply > 0, "empty")

    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    let bps: u64 = current_fee_bps(graduated)
    let gross: u64 = sell_xel_out(reserves, curve_supply, token_amount)
    require(gross >= 1, "tiny")
    let fee: u64 = fee_take(gross, bps)
    let out: u64 = gross - fee
    require(out >= 1, "tinyout")
    require(reserves >= gross, "curverr")

    // Curve state (tokens return to the curve, gross XEL leaves reserves).
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES), reserves - gross)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE), curve_supply + token_amount)
    s.store(bkey, bal - token_amount)

    // Accounting (D12): sell-side volume uses the PRE-FEE gross, exactly
    // like the legacy total (vo) always did.
    record_trade(pid, false, gross)
    let curve_xel: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    require(curve_xel >= gross, "accerr")
    s.store(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY, curve_xel - gross)
    if fee > 0 {
        let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending + fee)
    }

    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    let ok: bool = transfer(caller, out, xel)
    require(ok, "txfail")

    emit_event(EV_TOKENS_SOLD, [pid.to_string(10u32), token_amount.to_string(10u32), out.to_string(10u32), fee.to_string(10u32)])

    // D12 — stored market cap follows every curve state change.
    update_market_cap(pid)
    return out
}

// ============================================================================
// 22. CLAIM REFUND — the founder's exit on a REJECTED project.
// ============================================================================
// Only for a project that FAILED its initial validation, only by the
// creator, exactly once: 100% of the deposited liquidity is returned.
// (Projects that reached trading can never be "rejected" — the curve's XEL
// then belongs to the market, not to the founder alone.)
// ============================================================================
entry claim_refund(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status == ST_REJECTED, "norefund")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    require(creator_opt.is_some(), "nocr")
    let creator: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == creator, "notauth")

    require(s.load(proj_key(pid, F_REFUND)).unwrap_or(false) == false, "claimed")
    let liquidity: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_REFUND), true)

    let locked: u64 = s.load(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    require(locked >= liquidity, "accerr")
    s.store(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY, locked - liquidity)

    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    let ok: bool = transfer(caller, liquidity, xel)
    require(ok, "txfail")

    emit_event(EV_REFUND_CLAIMED, [pid.to_string(10u32), liquidity.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 23. REQUEST REVALIDATION — the creator's path back from Untrusted.
// ============================================================================
// Opens a fresh voting window (tallies and the voted-map reset via a new
// round number). For a project that already graduated, the recovery_fee is
// charged (attached deposit must equal it EXACTLY — it goes to the admin
// via pending_fees) and the STRICTER thresholds apply at finalization.
// Non-graduated projects retry for free under normal thresholds.
// ============================================================================
entry request_revalidation(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status == ST_UNTRUSTED, "badstate")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    require(creator_opt.is_some(), "nocr")
    let creator: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == creator, "notauth")

    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    if graduated {
        let recovery_fee: u64 = s.load(RECOVERY_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_FEE)
        let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
        let dep: u64 = get_deposit_for_asset(xel).unwrap_or(0)
        require(dep == recovery_fee, "badfee")
        if recovery_fee > 0 {
            let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
            s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending + recovery_fee)
        }
    }

    let round: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND), round + 1)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS), 0u64)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS), 0u64)
    let duration: u64 = s.load(VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VALIDATION_TOPO)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE), get_current_topoheight() + duration)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS), ST_RECOVERY)

    emit_event(EV_RECOVERY_REQUESTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), (round + 1).to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 24. UPDATE PROJECT INFO — metadata maintenance (creator only).
// ============================================================================
// Description, website, logo AND the social links (D11) can be updated at
// any time (except on a Rejected project) — communities move, channels get
// rebuilt; name, symbol, supply, team allocation and the vesting plan are
// structural and immutable by design (the plan is the votable commitment,
// D10 — changing it after the vote would be changing the ballot).
// ============================================================================
entry update_project_info(pid: u64, description: string, website: string, logo: string, twitter: string, telegram: string, discord: string) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(status != ST_REJECTED, "dead")

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    require(creator_opt.is_some(), "nocr")
    let creator: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == creator, "notauth")

    require(description.len() <= MAX_DESC_LEN, "baddesc")
    require(website.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badurl")
    require(logo.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badlogo")
    require(twitter.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badtw")
    require(telegram.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "badtg")
    require(discord.len() <= MAX_URL_LEN, "baddc")

    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DESC), description)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_WEBSITE), website)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_LOGO), logo)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TWITTER), twitter)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TELEGRAM), telegram)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_DISCORD), discord)

    emit_event(EV_PROJECT_INFO_UPDATED, [pid.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 25. START TEAM VESTING — the creator's voluntary long-term commitment.
// ============================================================================
// @caller: the project creator (a wallet).
// @params: duration — linear vesting length in topoheights, within the
//          admin-bounded window [vesting_min, vesting_max].
// @rules:  eligible once the allocation is unlockable at all: after
//          graduation (immediately), or for a never-graduated project after
//          team_unlock_delay of bonding (D3). Once started, the vesting is
//          IRREVERSIBLE — that is the point: it is a public commitment the
//          frontend can show (get_team_allocation). No partial claim before
//          the stream starts paying. NOT available to projects that
//          declared a vesting plan at propose time (D10): the plan binds
//          itself at graduation — exactly the schedule the community voted
//          on, no re-tuning possible.
// ============================================================================
entry start_team_vesting(pid: u64, duration: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    require(creator_opt.is_some(), "nocr")
    let creator: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == creator, "notauth")

    // D10: a declared plan IS the vesting — it starts by itself at
    // graduation and can be neither replaced nor duplicated.
    require(s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_PLAN)).unwrap_or(0) == 0, "planned")

    // Exactly one vesting per project, and only while something is owed.
    require(s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START)).unwrap_or(0) == 0, "started")
    require(team_remaining(pid) > 0, "done")

    let min_dur: u64 = s.load(VESTING_MIN_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MIN)
    let max_dur: u64 = s.load(VESTING_MAX_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MAX)
    require(duration >= min_dur && duration <= max_dur, "baddur")

    // Eligibility mirrors claim_team_allocation (D3): the allocation must
    // be unlockable NOW (graduated, or bonding past the unlock delay).
    require(team_unlocked(pid) > 0, "notyet")

    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START), get_current_topoheight())
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_DURATION), duration)

    emit_event(EV_TEAM_VESTING_STARTED, [pid.to_string(10u32), duration.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 26. CLAIM TEAM ALLOCATION — the creator's payout, all paths, once (I4).
// ============================================================================
// @caller: the project creator (a wallet).
// @rules:  pays team_unlocked(pid) - team_paid:
//            * vesting active  -> the linear share accrued so far (D3);
//            * graduated       -> the full remaining allocation (the
//                                 migration reward), unless a vesting is
//                                 running (then only the accrued share);
//            * never graduated -> the full allocation, but only after
//                                 team_unlock_delay of bonding (the late
//                                 claim — founders are never hostage);
//            * otherwise (Validation / Rejected / too early) -> revert.
//          team_paid debits every payout, so the allocation is paid exactly
//          once across ALL paths (I4).
// ============================================================================
entry claim_team_allocation(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    require(creator_opt.is_some(), "nocr")
    let creator: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == creator, "notauth")

    let unlocked: u64 = team_unlocked(pid)
    let paid: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_PAID)).unwrap_or(0)
    require(unlocked > paid, "nothing")

    let pay: u64 = unlocked - paid
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_PAID), paid + pay)

    let bkey: string = bal_key(pid, creator)
    let bal: u64 = s.load(bkey).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(bkey, bal + pay)

    // D12 — a claim shrinks team_remaining, i.e. GROWS circulating supply:
    // the stored market cap follows immediately (it must never lag a state
    // change of the curve's inputs — reserves, curve supply, team_paid).
    update_market_cap(pid)

    emit_event(EV_TEAM_CLAIMED, [pid.to_string(10u32), pay.to_string(10u32)])
    return pay
}

// ============================================================================
// ADMIN — parameter setters (all range-checked, pairs cross-checked) + fee
// withdrawal.
// ============================================================================

// 27. Submission fee (one-time, per proposal). Cap: 100 XEL.
entry set_submission_fee(fee: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(fee <= MAX_SUBMISSION_FEE, "toohigh")
    s.store(SUBMISSION_FEE_KEY, fee)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["submission_fee", fee.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 28. Trading fee in basis points, on buys AND sells while bonding.
//     Hard cap: 10%. Cross-checked (D8): can never drop below the
//     graduated fee — graduation must always be the cheaper regime.
entry set_trading_fee(bps: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(bps <= MAX_TRADING_FEE_BPS, "toohigh")
    let graduated_fee: u64 = s.load(GRADUATED_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS)
    require(bps >= graduated_fee, "croserr")
    s.store(TRADING_FEE_KEY, bps)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["trading_fee_bps", bps.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 29. Graduated trading fee (D8): what a graduated project pays on every
//     trade. Hard cap: 10%. Cross-checked: <= trading_fee_bps, so the
//     graduation discount can never invert.
entry set_graduated_trading_fee(bps: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(bps <= MAX_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS, "toohigh")
    let trading_fee: u64 = s.load(TRADING_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS)
    require(bps <= trading_fee, "croserr")
    s.store(GRADUATED_FEE_KEY, bps)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["graduated_fee_bps", bps.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 30. Migration fee (D9): taken once from a project's reserves when it
//     graduates (curve path or direct listing). Hard cap: 5%.
entry set_migration_fee(bps: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(bps <= MAX_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS, "toohigh")
    s.store(MIGRATION_FEE_KEY, bps)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["migration_fee_bps", bps.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 31. Direct-listing threshold (D7): the liquidity that skips the bonding
//     phase. Cross-checked: >= min_liquidity, so the fast track can never
//     swallow every proposal (a small float always gets its curve).
//     Snapshotted per project at propose time.
entry set_direct_listing_threshold(amount: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(amount <= MAX_DIRECT_LISTING, "toohigh")
    let min_liq: u64 = s.load(MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_LIQUIDITY)
    require(amount >= min_liq, "croserr")
    s.store(DIRECT_LISTING_KEY, amount)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["direct_listing_threshold", amount.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 32. Minimum founder liquidity, in [1 XEL, 100k XEL]. Cross-checked
//     (D7): can never exceed the direct-listing threshold.
entry set_min_liquidity(amount: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(amount >= MIN_LIQUIDITY_FLOOR, "toolow")
    require(amount <= MAX_MIN_LIQUIDITY, "toohigh")
    let threshold: u64 = s.load(DIRECT_LISTING_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_DIRECT_LISTING)
    require(amount <= threshold, "croserr")
    s.store(MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY, amount)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["min_liquidity", amount.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 33. Minimum voters to validate/reject a project, in [1, 100k].
entry set_min_participants(count: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(count >= 1, "toolow")
    require(count <= MAX_PARTICIPANTS, "toohigh")
    s.store(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY, count)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["min_participants", count.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 34. Minimum support ratio, in (50%, 100%] basis points.
entry set_min_approval_ratio(bps: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(bps >= MIN_RATIO_BPS, "toolow")
    require(bps <= 10000, "toohigh")
    s.store(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY, bps)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["min_approval_ratio_bps", bps.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 35. Validation window length in topoheights, [~1h, ~15d].
entry set_validation_duration(topos: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(topos >= MIN_VALIDATION_TOPO, "toolow")
    require(topos <= MAX_VALIDATION_TOPO, "toohigh")
    s.store(VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY, topos)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["validation_duration", topos.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 36. Graduation multiplier: graduate at liquidity x multiplier, [2, 100].
entry set_graduation_multiplier(multiplier: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(multiplier >= MIN_GRAD_MULTIPLIER, "toolow")
    require(multiplier <= MAX_GRAD_MULTIPLIER, "toohigh")
    s.store(GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY, multiplier)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["graduation_multiplier", multiplier.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 37. Team unlock delay (D3): how long a NEVER-graduated project must
//     trade before its creator may claim the team allocation late.
//     [~5 days, ~2 years].
entry set_team_unlock_delay(topos: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(topos >= MIN_TEAM_DELAY_TOPO, "toolow")
    require(topos <= MAX_TEAM_DELAY_TOPO, "toohigh")
    s.store(TEAM_DELAY_KEY, topos)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["team_unlock_delay", topos.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 38. Vesting bounds (D3): the window inside which a creator may choose a
//     linear vesting duration. Absolute caps: [~1 day, ~2 years]; the
//     window itself must stay non-empty (min < max).
entry set_vesting_bounds(min_topos: u64, max_topos: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(min_topos >= VESTING_FLOOR_TOPO, "toolow")
    require(max_topos <= VESTING_CEIL_TOPO, "toohigh")
    require(min_topos < max_topos, "croserr")
    s.store(VESTING_MIN_KEY, min_topos)
    s.store(VESTING_MAX_KEY, max_topos)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["vesting_bounds", min_topos.to_string(10u32) + ":" + max_topos.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 39. Recovery fee for GRADUATED projects requesting revalidation.
//     Cap: 1000 XEL. (Non-graduated projects always retry for free.)
entry set_recovery_fee(fee: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(fee <= MAX_RECOVERY_FEE, "toohigh")
    s.store(RECOVERY_FEE_KEY, fee)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["recovery_fee", fee.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 40. Stricter recovery thresholds: quorum in [1, 100k], ratio in (50%, 100%].
entry set_recovery_params(participants: u64, ratio_bps: u64) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require(participants >= 1, "toolow")
    require(participants <= MAX_PARTICIPANTS, "toohigh")
    require(ratio_bps >= MIN_RATIO_BPS, "toolow")
    require(ratio_bps <= 10000, "toohigh")
    s.store(RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS_KEY, participants)
    s.store(RECOVERY_RATIO_KEY, ratio_bps)
    emit_event(EV_PARAM_SET, ["recovery_params", participants.to_string(10u32) + ":" + ratio_bps.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// 41. Transfer the admin role (single-step — use a cold wallet).
entry set_admin(new_admin: Address) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    s.store(ADMIN_KEY, new_admin)
    emit_event(EV_ADMIN_SET, [new_admin.to_string()])
    return 0
}

// 42. Circuit breaker: pauses NEW proposals and NEW buys only (D-security).
//     Sells, votes, refunds, team claims and finalization are never pausable.
entry set_paused(flag: bool) -> u64 {
    only_admin()
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    s.store(PAUSED_KEY, flag)
    if flag {
        emit_event(EV_PAUSED, ["admin"])
    } else {
        emit_event(EV_UNPAUSED, ["admin"])
    }
    return 0
}

// 43. WITHDRAW FEES — the protocol's entire revenue stream.
// ============================================================================
// Admin-only. Capped twice: by the accrued pending_fees AND by the
// contract's uncommitted balance (balance - curve commitments - refundable
// rejections) — the admin can never make the protocol insolvent (I2).
// ============================================================================
entry withdraw_fees(amount: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()

    let caller_opt: optional<Address> = get_caller()
    require(caller_opt.is_some(), "walletonly")
    let caller: Address = caller_opt.expect("guarded")

    let admin_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(ADMIN_KEY)
    require(admin_opt.is_some(), "noadmin")
    let admin: Address = admin_opt.expect("guarded")
    require(caller == admin, "notauth")

    require(amount > 0, "badamt")
    let pending: u64 = s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    require(amount <= pending, "badamt")

    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    let balance: u64 = get_balance_for_asset(xel).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_xel: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let locked: u64 = s.load(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let committed: u128 = (curve_xel as u128) + (locked as u128)
    require((amount as u128) + committed <= (balance as u128), "notavail")

    s.store(PENDING_FEES_KEY, pending - amount)
    let lifetime: u64 = s.load(FEES_LIFETIME_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(FEES_LIFETIME_KEY, lifetime + amount)

    let ok: bool = transfer(caller, amount, xel)
    require(ok, "txfail")

    emit_event(EV_FEES_COLLECTED, [amount.to_string(10u32)])
    return 0
}

// ============================================================================
// 44. CHECKED ADD — u64 + u64 with an explicit overflow refusal (I9's
//     arithmetic backbone). The volume accumulators are the only counters in
//     the contract that grow without bound by design, so every addition on
//     them goes through this: unreachable in practice (a u64 volume at the
//     10 000 XEL per-trade cap would need ~18 million full-size trades),
//     guarded anyway — a corrupted counter is worse than a refused trade.
//     (Declared AFTER the entries on purpose: chunks 16..43 are the entry
//     ids real transactions are built from — keeping them byte-stable
//     across versions is worth the forward references below.)
// ============================================================================
fn checked_add(a: u64, b: u64) -> u64 {
    let wide: u128 = (a as u128) + (b as u128)
    require(wide <= U64_MAX_128, "ovf")
    return wide as u64
}

// ============================================================================
// 45. UPDATE MARKET CAP (D12) — recompute the spot market cap from the
//     curve's live state (same formula as the pure get_market_cap view) and
//     STORE it: mc = current spot, mh = all-time high (monotone). Idempotent
//     by construction — it derives everything from storage, never from
//     its own previous output, so calling it twice in one entry (graduate
//     then the closing update_market_cap of buy) is a harmless no-op write.
// ============================================================================
fn update_market_cap(pid: u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    let cap: u64 = 0
    if curve_supply > 0 {
        let team_rem: u128 = team_remaining(pid) as u128
        let circulating: u128 = (total_supply as u128) - (curve_supply as u128) - team_rem
        if circulating > 0 {
            let wide: u128 = (reserves as u128) * circulating / (curve_supply as u128)
            if wide <= U64_MAX_128 {
                cap = wide as u64
            } else {
                cap = U64_MAX
            }
        }
    }
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP), cap)
    let high: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_HIGH)).unwrap_or(0)
    if cap > high {
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_HIGH), cap)
    }
}

// ============================================================================
// 46. RECORD TRADE (D12) — the single funnel through which every buy/sell
//     updates the scoreboard, so the volume identity (I9) holds by
//     construction: vo only ever grows here, by exactly the recorded amount,
//     and bv/sv partition the trades. Also bumps trade counts and stamps the
//     last-trade topoheight. Buy side records the ATTACHED amount (fee
//     included — an exchange's quote-side convention); sell side records the
//     PRE-FEE gross out; exactly the two quantities the v1 total always
//     summed. update_market_cap is also called from claim_team_allocation:
//     a claim changes circulating supply, and the stored cap must never lag
//     ANY input of its formula (reserves, curve supply, team_paid).
// ============================================================================
fn record_trade(pid: u64, buy_side: bool, xel_amount: u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    if buy_side {
        let bv: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_BUY_VOL)).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_BUY_VOL), checked_add(bv, xel_amount))
        let tbv: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_BUY_VOL_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(TOTAL_BUY_VOL_KEY, checked_add(tbv, xel_amount))
    } else {
        let sv: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SELL_VOL)).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(proj_key(pid, F_SELL_VOL), checked_add(sv, xel_amount))
        let tsv: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_SELL_VOL_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
        s.store(TOTAL_SELL_VOL_KEY, checked_add(tsv, xel_amount))
    }
    let vo: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VOLUME)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_VOLUME), checked_add(vo, xel_amount))
    let tvl: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY, checked_add(tvl, xel_amount))
    let tc: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TRADES)).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_TRADES), checked_add(tc, 1))
    let ttc: u64 = s.load(TOTAL_TRADES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    s.store(TOTAL_TRADES_KEY, checked_add(ttc, 1))
    s.store(proj_key(pid, F_LAST_TRADE), get_current_topoheight())
}

// ============================================================================
// VIEWS (pub fn — read-only, no storage writes; the frontend's API)
// ============================================================================

// 47. Lifecycle snapshot: (creator, status, created_topo, validation_end,
//     graduated). creator is a display string; status is the code (see
//     get_status_label).
pub fn get_project(pid: u64) -> (string, u64, u64, u64, bool) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)

    let creator: string = "unknown"
    let creator_opt: optional<Address> = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATOR))
    if creator_opt.is_some() {
        let c: Address = creator_opt.expect("guarded")
        creator = c.to_string()
    }

    return (
        creator,
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATED)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    )
}

// 48. Display metadata: (name, symbol, description, website, logo).
pub fn get_project_info(pid: u64) -> (string, string, string, string, string) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_NAME)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SYMBOL)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DESC)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_WEBSITE)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LOGO)).unwrap_or("")
    )
}

// 49. Status code of a project (see get_status_label for the text).
pub fn get_project_status(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return s.load(proj_key(pid, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
}

// 50. Tokenomics: (total_supply, team_bps, liquidity_deposited, reserves,
//     curve_supply). All atomic units.
pub fn get_project_tokenomics(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 51. Trust state: (supports, reports, vote_round, graduated).
pub fn get_project_trust(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, bool) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPORTS)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_REPORTS)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    )
}

// 52. Curve state: (reserves, curve_supply, volume, graduation_target,
//     bonding_start). graduation_target = liquidity_deposited *
//     graduation_multiplier (the curve path's goal; a direct-listed project
//     starts beyond it). bonding_start = when trading opened (0 while in
//     validation) — the anchor of the team unlock delay.
pub fn get_bonding_info(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let liquidity: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let multiplier: u64 = s.load(GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRAD_MULTIPLIER)
    let target: u128 = (liquidity as u128) * (multiplier as u128)
    let grad_target: u64 = U64_MAX
    if target <= U64_MAX_128 {
        grad_target = target as u64
    }
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VOLUME)).unwrap_or(0),
        grad_target,
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_BONDING_START)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 53. Spot price: XEL (scaled by 1e8) per 1 whole token — i.e.
//     reserves * 1e8 / curve_supply. Frontends divide the display token
//     amount by 1e8 exactly like XEL amounts. Saturates at u64 max.
pub fn get_current_price(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    if curve_supply == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    let scaled: u128 = (reserves as u128) * (PRICE_SCALE as u128) / (curve_supply as u128)
    if scaled > U64_MAX_128 {
        return U64_MAX
    }
    return scaled as u64
}

// 54. Buy quote: tokens out for an attached XEL amount (fee included).
//     Uses the project's EFFECTIVE fee (graduated rate once graduated —
//     D8), exactly like buy() — a quote can never disagree with the trade.
pub fn get_buy_quote(pid: u64, xel_amount: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    let bps: u64 = current_fee_bps(graduated)
    let net: u64 = xel_amount - fee_take(xel_amount, bps)
    return buy_tokens_out(reserves, curve_supply, net)
}

// 55. Sell quote: XEL out (net of fee) for a token amount — same effective
//     fee rule as sell().
pub fn get_sell_quote(pid: u64, token_amount: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    let graduated: bool = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_GRADUATED)).unwrap_or(false)
    let bps: u64 = current_fee_bps(graduated)
    let gross: u64 = sell_xel_out(reserves, curve_supply, token_amount)
    return gross - fee_take(gross, bps)
}

// 56. Market cap in atomic XEL: reserves * circulating / curve_supply,
//     where circulating = total_supply - curve_supply - team_remaining
//     (the allocation not yet paid to the creator). Saturates at u64 max
//     (u128 math throughout).
pub fn get_market_cap(pid: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let reserves: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_RESERVES)).unwrap_or(0)
    let curve_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CURVE)).unwrap_or(0)
    if curve_supply == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    let team_rem: u128 = team_remaining(pid) as u128
    let circulating: u128 = (total_supply as u128) - (curve_supply as u128) - team_rem
    if circulating == 0 {
        return 0
    }
    let cap: u128 = (reserves as u128) * circulating / (curve_supply as u128)
    if cap > U64_MAX_128 {
        return U64_MAX
    }
    return cap as u64
}

// 57. Token balance of an address (atomic units) — the launched token IS
//     this internal ledger (D1); frontends display it like any balance.
pub fn get_token_balance(pid: u64, owner: Address) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return s.load(bal_key(pid, owner)).unwrap_or(0)
}

// 58. Has this address already voted in the project's CURRENT round?
pub fn has_voted(pid: u64, voter: Address) -> bool {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let round: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_ROUND)).unwrap_or(0)
    return s.load(vote_key(pid, round, voter)).unwrap_or(false)
}

// 59. Total number of projects ever proposed.
pub fn get_total_projects() -> u64 {
    return Storage::new().load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
}

// 60. COUNT of projects with a given status code (listing helper — pair
//     with get_project_by_rank; ids themselves are never returned as an
//     array, Silex ABI ground truth has no array returns).
pub fn get_projects_by_status(status: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let count: u64 = s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let found: u64 = 0
    for i: u64 = 0; i < MAX_PROJECTS; i += 1 {
        if i < count {
            if s.load(proj_key(i, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0) == status {
                found += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return found
}

// 61. Id of the rank-th (0-based, oldest first) project with a given
//     status. Returns project_count (an invalid id) when rank is out of
//     range — the documented sentinel for "no such project".
pub fn get_project_by_rank(status: u64, rank: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let count: u64 = s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let seen: u64 = 0
    for i: u64 = 0; i < MAX_PROJECTS; i += 1 {
        if i < count {
            if s.load(proj_key(i, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0) == status {
                if seen == rank {
                    return i
                }
                seen += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return count
}

// 62. Id of the rank-th LATEST project (any status; rank 0 = newest).
//     Sentinel: project_count when out of range.
pub fn get_latest_projects(rank: u64) -> u64 {
    let count: u64 = Storage::new().load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    if rank < count {
        return count - 1 - rank
    }
    return count
}

// 63. COUNT of trusted projects (Graduated or Trusted — both mean the
//     community currently backs the project).
pub fn get_trusted_projects() -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let count: u64 = s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let found: u64 = 0
    for i: u64 = 0; i < MAX_PROJECTS; i += 1 {
        if i < count {
            let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(i, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
            if status == ST_GRADUATED || status == ST_TRUSTED {
                found += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return found
}

// 64. Id of the rank-th trusted (Graduated/Trusted) project, oldest first.
//     Sentinel: project_count when out of range.
pub fn get_trusted_by_rank(rank: u64) -> u64 {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let count: u64 = s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    let seen: u64 = 0
    for i: u64 = 0; i < MAX_PROJECTS; i += 1 {
        if i < count {
            let status: u64 = s.load(proj_key(i, F_STATUS)).unwrap_or(0)
            if status == ST_GRADUATED || status == ST_TRUSTED {
                if seen == rank {
                    return i
                }
                seen += 1
            }
        }
    }
    return count
}

// 65. TEAM ALLOCATION STATE (D3, D10) — the frontend's commitment panel:
//     (team_alloc, team_paid, vesting_start, vesting_duration,
//      claimable_now, vesting_plan). vesting_start == 0 means no vesting is
//      running; vesting_plan == 0 means "claim at graduation" was declared,
//      any other value is the plan graduate() binds automatically (D10) —
//      show it on the proposal card BEFORE the vote. claimable_now is
//      exactly what claim_team_allocation would pay at the current
//      topoheight (0 = nothing yet — show a countdown).
pub fn get_team_allocation(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    let total_supply: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team_bps: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0)
    let team: u64 = team_alloc_of(total_supply, team_bps)
    let paid: u64 = s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_PAID)).unwrap_or(0)
    let unlocked: u64 = team_unlocked(pid)
    let claimable: u64 = 0
    if unlocked > paid {
        claimable = unlocked - paid
    }
    return (
        team,
        paid,
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_START)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_DURATION)).unwrap_or(0),
        claimable,
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_PLAN)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 66. Protocol stats: (total_projects, pending_fees, fees_collected_lifetime,
//     total_volume, total_curve_xel, locked_refunds, balance, paused,
//     trading_fee_bps). balance is the live contract XEL balance — the
//     solvency invariant says it covers curve_xel + pending + locked.
pub fn get_protocol_stats() -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, bool, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    let xel: Hash = s.load(XEL_ASSET_KEY).unwrap_or(get_xelis_asset())
    return (
        s.load(COUNT_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(PENDING_FEES_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(FEES_LIFETIME_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(TOTAL_CURVE_XEL_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(LOCKED_REFUNDS_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        get_balance_for_asset(xel).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(PAUSED_KEY).unwrap_or(false),
        s.load(TRADING_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS)
    )
}

// 67. Launch parameter set: (submission_fee, min_liquidity, trading_fee_bps,
//     graduated_fee_bps, min_participants, min_approval_ratio_bps,
//     validation_duration, graduation_multiplier, direct_listing_threshold,
//     migration_fee_bps). Recovery and team parameters live in their own
//     views (get_recovery_config / get_team_config).
pub fn get_config() -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    return (
        s.load(SUBMISSION_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_SUBMISSION_FEE),
        s.load(MIN_LIQUIDITY_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_LIQUIDITY),
        s.load(TRADING_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TRADING_FEE_BPS),
        s.load(GRADUATED_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRADUATED_FEE_BPS),
        s.load(MIN_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_PARTICIPANTS),
        s.load(MIN_APPROVAL_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIN_APPROVAL_BPS),
        s.load(VALIDATION_DURATION_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VALIDATION_TOPO),
        s.load(GRAD_MULTIPLIER_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_GRAD_MULTIPLIER),
        s.load(DIRECT_LISTING_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_DIRECT_LISTING),
        s.load(MIGRATION_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_MIGRATION_FEE_BPS)
    )
}

// 68. Recovery parameter set: (recovery_fee, recovery_min_participants,
//     recovery_min_ratio_bps).
pub fn get_recovery_config() -> (u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    return (
        s.load(RECOVERY_FEE_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_FEE),
        s.load(RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_PARTICIPANTS),
        s.load(RECOVERY_RATIO_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_RECOVERY_RATIO_BPS)
    )
}

// 69. Team parameter set: (team_unlock_delay, vesting_min, vesting_max),
//     all in topoheights (D3).
pub fn get_team_config() -> (u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    return (
        s.load(TEAM_DELAY_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_TEAM_DELAY),
        s.load(VESTING_MIN_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MIN),
        s.load(VESTING_MAX_KEY).unwrap_or(DEFAULT_VESTING_MAX)
    )
}

// 70. SOCIAL LINKS (D11): (twitter, telegram, discord) — empty string
//     means "no link". Updatable by the creator at any time via
//     update_project_info; the frontend renders, the voters judge.
pub fn get_social_links(pid: u64) -> (string, string, string) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TWITTER)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TELEGRAM)).unwrap_or(""),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DISCORD)).unwrap_or("")
    )
}

// 71. TRADING STATS (D12): (buy_volume, sell_volume, total_volume,
//     trade_count, last_trade_topo) — the project's on-chain scoreboard,
//     maintained by record_trade on every buy/sell. buy_volume sums the
//     attached XEL of every buy (fee included); sell_volume sums the pre-fee
//     gross of every sell; total == buy + sell (I9). last_trade_topo == 0
//     means the project never traded.
pub fn get_trading_stats(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_BUY_VOL)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SELL_VOL)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VOLUME)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TRADES)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LAST_TRADE)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 72. MARKET CAP HISTORY (D12): (current, all_time_high, at_graduation) —
//     the stored series maintained by update_market_cap / graduate. current
//     is rewritten after every trade with the same formula as the pure
//     get_market_cap view; all_time_high only ever grows; at_graduation is
//     snapshotted once, after the migration fee (0 = never graduated, OR a
//     direct listing at t0 — nothing is circulating before the first buy,
//     so the honest snapshot is 0; mc/mh light up on the first trade).
//     All in atomic XEL.
pub fn get_market_cap_history(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_HIGH)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_MCAP_GRAD)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 73. PROPOSAL DATA (D10, D7) — the ONE-CALL voting card: everything the
//     community needs to judge a proposal BEFORE the vote, in one view:
//     (liquidity, total_supply, team_bps, vesting_plan, direct_listed,
//      created_topo, validation_end). vesting_plan == 0 -> the team claims
//     at graduation; any other value is the linear vesting the contract
//     will bind at graduation (the votable commitment). direct_listed is
//     the D7 snapshot: liquidity >= threshold at propose time -> graduates
//     the moment validation passes (no bonding phase). Metadata lives in
//     get_project_info / get_social_links; live curve numbers in
//     get_project_tokenomics / get_bonding_info / get_current_price.
pub fn get_proposal_data(pid: u64) -> (u64, u64, u64, u64, bool, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    require_project(pid)
    return (
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_LIQUIDITY)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_SUPPLY)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_TEAM_BPS)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_VESTING_PLAN)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DL)).unwrap_or(false),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_CREATED)).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(proj_key(pid, F_DEADLINE)).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 74. PROTOCOL VOLUME STATS (D12): (total_volume, total_buy_volume,
//     total_sell_volume, total_trades) across every project ever launched —
//     the launchpad's own scoreboard. total == buy + sell (I9).
pub fn get_volume_stats() -> (u64, u64, u64, u64) {
    let s: Storage = Storage::new()
    return (
        s.load(TOTAL_VOLUME_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(TOTAL_BUY_VOL_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(TOTAL_SELL_VOL_KEY).unwrap_or(0),
        s.load(TOTAL_TRADES_KEY).unwrap_or(0)
    )
}

// 75. Human-readable status label (frontend convenience).
pub fn get_status_label(status: u64) -> string {
    if status == ST_VALIDATION {
        return "validation"
    }
    if status == ST_REJECTED {
        return "rejected"
    }
    if status == ST_BONDING {
        return "bonding"
    }
    if status == ST_GRADUATED {
        return "graduated"
    }
    if status == ST_TRUSTED {
        return "trusted"
    }
    if status == ST_UNTRUSTED {
        return "untrusted"
    }
    if status == ST_RECOVERY {
        return "recovery"
    }
    return "unknown"
}

// 76. Contract version.
pub fn get_version() -> string {
    return VERSION
}
